    { q: 'Is one week enough to study for an exam?', a: 'For a unit test or mid-term, usually yes. For a final covering a whole term, one week is enough to secure the most important topics and practise exam questions, but not to master everything. Triage on day 1 is what makes the week work.' },
    { q: 'How many hours a day should I study in the last week?', a: 'Four to six focused hours, in 45–60 minute blocks with breaks, is realistic for most students. More than that usually turns into tired rereading.' },
    { q: 'Should I pull an all-nighter before the exam?', a: 'No. Research on high-school students found that giving up sleep to study more than usual led to more academic problems the next day. Sleep also helps your brain keep what you studied.' },
